  <static seed="34" source="Contrib/CCCS/AlgebraicLiteracy/IA_7.2/OpenStax_IA_7.2_121.pg">
    <statement><p>Add or subtract the rational expressions.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{{\frac{t}{t-3}} - {\frac{t+9}{t+3}} = }</m><fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{-3t+27}{\left(t+3\right)\mathopen{}\left(t-3\right)}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>The LCD must contain each factor from each denominator, so the LCD = <m>{\left(t+3\right)\mathopen{}\left(t-3\right)}</m>.</p>
<p>We need to rewrite each expression with the LCD:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ {\frac{t}{t-3}} \cdot \frac{t+3}{t+3} - {\frac{t+9}{t+3}} \cdot \frac{t-3}{t-3} }</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \frac{{t^{2}+3t}}{{\left(t+3\right)\mathopen{}\left(t-3\right)}} - \frac{{t^{2}+9t-3t-27}}{{\left(t+3\right)\mathopen{}\left(t-3\right)}} }</m></p>
<p>Notice the subtraction applies to every term in the 2nd fraction:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{\frac{{t^{2}+3t}}{{\left(t+3\right)\mathopen{}\left(t-3\right)}} + \frac{{-t^{2}-6t+27}}{{\left(t+3\right)\mathopen{}\left(t-3\right)}}}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{{\frac{-3t+27}{\left(t+3\right)\mathopen{}\left(t-3\right)}}}</m></p>
</solution>
